# ===========================================================================
# samples/demo.log - synthetic capture used by the docs, the CLI examples
# and tests/test_cli.py. Three formats in one file, on purpose:
#
#   1. Linux auth.log   (syslog framed SSH / PAM events)
#   2. Nginx access log (Combined Log Format)
#   3. RFC3164 syslog   (UFW firewall blocks)
#
# Nothing here is real data; every IP lives in the RFC 5737 documentation
# ranges (192.0.2.0/24, 198.51.100.0/24, 203.0.113.0/24) and the internal
# host uses 10.0.0.0/8.
#
# Expected result (default --threshold 5):
#   36 parsed events, 7 threats
#   (CRITICAL 1 | HIGH 4 | MEDIUM 2 | LOW 0), riskiest 203.0.113.45 (92/100)
# ===========================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. SSH brute force against root, followed by a successful login.
#    6 failures inside 28s (>5 in 60s) then a success 13s later.
#    -> SSH_BRUTE_FORCE (HIGH) + SSH_BRUTE_FORCE_SUCCESS (CRITICAL)
#    35 + 45 + (6 failures x 2) = 92 risk points for 203.0.113.45
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
